(0) One is responsible for doing the work by hand in pencil of appropriate =
type on a printed version of the document (except if one uses appropriate t=
echnology or has software that allows one to write and also to draw straigh=
t line segments (that are visibly straight) on the pdf document directly wi=
th a stylus) and for uploading a legible copy on CANVAS as directed in the =
page How to Submit Assignments.

ONE IS REQUIRED TO SUBMIT A SINGLE PDF DOCUMENT WITH PROPER TITLE: YourName=
CourseNumberExamNX (as in AtishBagchi253Exam4P) exactly as shown. OTHERWISE=
 POINTS WILL BE DEDUCTED.

Computer labs at CCP campuses are open and students may print exams and sca=
n them there provided that they meet the critiera for visiting the campus.

(1) Read the General Information Document under Files which contains a long=
 section on exams, strategies for getting good grades, and what to concentr=
ate upon. It is one's responsibility to read all the material provided.

(2) Please print out a copy of the exam to use as rough copy or use a noteb=
ook to do work in rough. When one is ready to make a fair copy of the work,=
 one should print out a fresh copy and copy onto it. This should be picture=
 perfect. If there is any departure whatsoever from required format one wil=
l get a 0. If one submits incomplete or unchecked work one will get double =
the points (that a problem is worth) deducted. One needs to submit only wha=
t one has proved to be correct. One may not engage in guesswork or gambles =
unless obe wishes to be severely penalized.

(3) All work is done in the notes with many remarks to show how work is to =
be done. Under files one will find a folder entitled Solved Exams. It conta=
ins copies of previous exams with all the a and b problems worked out by a =
student. The format in these documents is absolutely correct. I will NOT in=
dicate if the solutions are correct because that is likely to lead to blind=
 copying, a habit that I do not wish to encourage. The J numbers are fictit=
ious. One's exams incidentally may be completely different from the solved =
ones.

(4) One must use rulers to draw ALL straight-line segments other than the o=
nes explicitly exempted on the top sheet of the exam. One has neither any f=
reedom not any choice regarding the matter. All signs of equality must be l=
ined up on the left as in the notes. All symbols must be used in precisely =
the intended senses and in no other. Please look at the document marked Sym=
bols under Files.

(5) Each time one finishes a problem completely, one must copy it onto the =
fair copy. It should not be left until the last minute. If one does all the=
 a problems completely correctly, one will have a decent chance of getting =
a C in the course. If one does all the a's and b's correctly, one will have=
 a good chance of getting an A in the course.

(6) Work should be shown on unruled sheets and the sheets should be numbere=
d as indicated on the exam. One may use the additional sheets that come wit=
h the exams if you change the page numbers to conform to the directions.

(7) The exams are available at all times. Note, however, that an exam can c=
ontinue to change to within two weeks of when it is due. Therefore, if one =
downloads an exam earlier than two weeks from when it is due, one needs to =
download it again two weeks before it is due.

